; S-05 persistent attention-forest operations — kernel/forms/helpers/forest.form
;
; Implements the seven forest helpers required by S-05/attention-alloc,
; per the spec in kernel/types/Forest.md (post-v0.1.1).
;
; Operations encoded here:
;
;   S-05/forest/get                       (ForestRoot, AttId)               → AttentionRecord
;   S-05/forest/new_child                 (AttId, Nat, CapId)               → AttId
;   S-05/forest/atomic_split              (ForestRoot, AttId, Nat, AttId, Nat) → ForestRoot
;   S-05/forest/dissolve_subtree_postorder (ForestRoot, AttId)              → Pair{ForestRoot, Vec{AttId}}
;   S-05/forest/deduct                    (ForestRoot, AttId, Nat)          → ForestRoot
;   S-05/forest/mark_yielded              (ForestRoot, AttId, Hash)         → ForestRoot
;   S-05/forest/set_deadline              (ForestRoot, AttId, Nat)          → ForestRoot
;
; Synthesis chain:
;   provocation:  STUBS.md catalogues seven S-05/forest/* helpers as
;                 pending; PR #30 closed the Forest.md spec gap. The
;                 encoding gap is the next step on the path to
;                 v0.2.5-ignis0-store, alongside the trie batch (PR #32).
;   grounding:    A0.5 (energy is finite — every operation is O(depth)
;                 over the HAMT keyed by AttId), A1.1/A1.4 (matter is
;                 content-addressed and shared by reference — the forest
;                 is persistent automatically), A3.2 (each mind owns a
;                 tree of attentions — the forest is the union of those
;                 trees), A3.5 (minds coexist — a forest, not a tree),
;                 A6.1 (code is substance). I6 (bounded epoch budget)
;                 is what the EOVERBUDGET checks below defend.
;   approach:     the forest is a HAMT instance (Forest.md § "Why a
;                 forest") parameterised on AttentionRecord leaves
;                 instead of Cell leaves. The seven public Forms read
;                 their ForestRoot argument, perform the budget / cap
;                 / presence checks that must be visible at the API
;                 surface (so the traps are declared on the public
;                 Form, not buried in a sub-helper), and delegate the
;                 HAMT walking and record reconstruction to the
;                 Forest/* and AttentionRecord/* schema sub-helpers.
;   composes_with:
;                 - kernel/types/Forest.md (the layout spec)
;                 - kernel/types/Trie.md (the shared HAMT primitives)
;                 - the encoded S-05/proj/* projections (cap_id,
;                   mind_id, budget_remaining, cap_view)
;                 - the AttentionRecord/* and Forest/* schema
;                   sub-helpers catalogued as pending in STUBS.md
;
; Helper exemption: each Form below exceeds the ~30-instruction
; smallness threshold of synthesis/PROTOCOL.md § Helper exemption, so
; each ships its own .proof obligation that S-08's walker recurses
; into; this file's footer drafts those obligations. The .proof
; artifact lands as a v0.2.0-helpers follow-up (ROADMAP action item 10),
; the same track as trie.proof.
;
; Pending leaves: every body below delegates to Forest/* and
; AttentionRecord/* schema sub-helpers that are NOT in this file —
; they are catalogued in STUBS.md and encoded in a subsequent
; forest-schema batch. Until that batch lands, the forest operations
; have pending leaves at every inner CALL, consistent with the
; layered convention from s04-projections.form and trie.form.

; ============================================================
; S-05/forest/get
;
; HAMT lookup of att_id. On hit returns the AttentionRecord hash
; carried by the matching ForestLeaf; on miss traps EUNHELD (the
; caller must already hold the attention it is asking about).
;
; Pseudocode:
;
;   get(root_h, att_id):
;     (found, record_h) = Forest/hamt_lookup(root_h, att_id)
;     if not found: trap EUNHELD
;     return record_h
; ============================================================

(form
  :type-tag      "Form/v1"
  :name          "forest_get"
  :declared-caps (S-05/FOREST_RW)
  :declared-traps (ETYPE EUNHELD)
  :arity         2
  :locals-n      6
  :code (
    STORE   0                            ; locals[0] := root_h (ForestRoot)
    STORE   1                            ; locals[1] := att_id (AttId)

    LOAD    0
    LOAD    1
    PUSH    "Forest/hamt_lookup"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=2                     ; → Pair{Bool, Hash}
    STORE   2                            ; locals[2] := lookup result

    LOAD    2
    FST                                  ; found?
    JMPZ    +get_miss
    LOAD    2
    SND                                  ; record_h
    RET

    :get_miss
    TRAP    EUNHELD
  )
  :rationale-hash $$BLAKE3$$/forest-rationale
)

; ============================================================
; S-05/forest/new_child
;
; A pure derivation — no ForestRoot argument. Returns the
; deterministic AttId a child would have under
; (parent_att_id, child_index, focus_cap_id):
;
;   child = BLAKE3("AttId" ‖ parent ‖ uleb128(index) ‖ focus)
;
; The seed never mints AttIds by RAND; every AttId is a function
; of its parent's AttId plus its index plus its focus, which makes
; the entire forest replayable from the Split weave entries
; (Forest.md § new_child). The tagged-hash construction itself is
; delegated to Forest/derive_att_id so the byte-layout rule lives
; in one place.
; ============================================================

(form
  :type-tag      "Form/v1"
  :name          "forest_new_child"
  :declared-caps (S-05/FOREST_RW)
  :declared-traps (ETYPE)
  :arity         3
  :locals-n      4
  :code (
    STORE   0                            ; locals[0] := parent_att_id (AttId)
    STORE   1                            ; locals[1] := child_index (Nat)
    STORE   2                            ; locals[2] := focus_cap_id (CapId)

    LOAD    0
    LOAD    1
    LOAD    2
    PUSH    "Forest/derive_att_id"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=3                     ; → child AttId
    RET
  )
  :rationale-hash $$BLAKE3$$/forest-rationale
)

; ============================================================
; S-05/forest/atomic_split
;
; Atomic "remove budget from parent + create child with that
; budget". Either both updates land or none do — there is no
; public helper that produces a half-applied forest (Forest.md
; § atomic_split, principle 3).
;
; Args: (root_h, parent_id, child_id, child_budget, child_deadline)
;
; Pseudocode:
;
;   atomic_split(root, parent_id, child_id, child_budget, child_deadline):
;     (found, parent_rec_h) = Forest/hamt_lookup(root, parent_id)
;     if not found: trap EUNHELD
;     parent_rec = read(parent_rec_h)
;     if parent_rec.budget_remaining < child_budget: trap EOVERBUDGET
;     child_rec  = AttentionRecord/construct_child(
;                      parent_id, parent_rec, child_budget, child_deadline)
;     parent_rec' = AttentionRecord/with_budget_sub_and_child(
;                      parent_rec, child_budget, child_id)
;     child_rec_h  = Forest/seal_record(child_rec)
;     parent_rec_h'= Forest/seal_record(parent_rec')
;     root'  = Forest/hamt_insert_record(root,  parent_id, parent_rec_h')
;     root'' = Forest/hamt_insert_record(root', child_id,  child_rec_h)
;     return root''
; ============================================================

(form
  :type-tag      "Form/v1"
  :name          "forest_atomic_split"
  :declared-caps (S-05/FOREST_RW)
  :declared-traps (ETYPE EUNHELD EOVERBUDGET)
  :arity         5
  :locals-n      14
  :code (
    STORE   0                            ; locals[0] := root_h
    STORE   1                            ; locals[1] := parent_id
    STORE   2                            ; locals[2] := child_id
    STORE   3                            ; locals[3] := child_budget (Nat)
    STORE   4                            ; locals[4] := child_deadline (Nat)

    ;; Locate the parent. Absent ⇒ EUNHELD.
    LOAD    0
    LOAD    1
    PUSH    "Forest/hamt_lookup"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=2                     ; → Pair{Bool, Hash}
    STORE   5
    LOAD    5
    FST
    JMPZ    +split_absent
    LOAD    5
    SND
    STORE   6                            ; locals[6] := parent_rec_h
    JMP     +split_present

    :split_absent
    TRAP    EUNHELD

    :split_present
    LOAD    6
    READ
    STORE   7                            ; locals[7] := parent_rec bytes

    ;; Budget guard: parent.budget_remaining < child_budget ⇒ EOVERBUDGET.
    LOAD    7
    PUSH    "S-05/proj/budget_remaining"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=1                     ; → parent.budget_remaining (Nat)
    LOAD    3                            ; child_budget
    LT                                   ; (budget < child_budget)?
    JMPZ    +split_ok
    TRAP    EOVERBUDGET

    :split_ok
    ;; Build the child record (inherits mind_id/cap_id/cap_view from
    ;; the parent record per Forest.md § atomic_split).
    LOAD    1                            ; parent_id
    LOAD    7                            ; parent_rec
    LOAD    3                            ; child_budget
    LOAD    4                            ; child_deadline
    PUSH    "AttentionRecord/construct_child"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=4                     ; → child_rec bytes
    STORE   8

    ;; Build the new parent record: budget -= child_budget, children
    ;; appended with child_id.
    LOAD    7                            ; parent_rec
    LOAD    3                            ; child_budget
    LOAD    2                            ; child_id
    PUSH    "AttentionRecord/with_budget_sub_and_child"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=3                     ; → parent_rec' bytes
    STORE   9

    ;; Seal both records.
    LOAD    8
    PUSH    "Forest/seal_record"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=1                     ; → child_rec_h
    STORE   10
    LOAD    9
    PUSH    "Forest/seal_record"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=1                     ; → parent_rec_h'
    STORE   11

    ;; Insert parent then child. Two persistent inserts; the second
    ;; threads the root produced by the first. Neither input root is
    ;; mutated, so the "atomic" guarantee is structural: only the
    ;; final root is observable to any caller.
    LOAD    0                            ; root
    LOAD    1                            ; parent_id
    LOAD    11                           ; parent_rec_h'
    PUSH    "Forest/hamt_insert_record"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=3                     ; → root'
    STORE   12
    LOAD    12                           ; root'
    LOAD    2                            ; child_id
    LOAD    10                           ; child_rec_h
    PUSH    "Forest/hamt_insert_record"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=3                     ; → root''
    RET
  )
  :rationale-hash $$BLAKE3$$/forest-rationale
)

; ============================================================
; S-05/forest/dissolve_subtree_postorder
;
; Walks the subtree rooted at att_id in postorder (children before
; parent), removes each visited record, and returns the new root
; together with the Vec{AttId} of removed ids in removal order. The
; caller emits one Dissolved{att_id} weave entry per id returned
; (S-05 proof obligation #4, "dissolution accounting").
;
; The postorder recursion lives in Forest/dissolve_rec — it reads
; the record's children list (AttentionRecord/proj/children),
; recurses on each child accumulating both the threaded root and
; the id vector, then removes the parent. This Form is the public
; entry point: it bottoms out the recursion and returns the pair.
;
; Pseudocode:
;
;   dissolve(root, att_id):
;     (found, _) = Forest/hamt_lookup(root, att_id)
;     if not found: return Pair{root, []}      ; idempotent
;     return Forest/dissolve_rec(root, att_id) ; postorder walk
; ============================================================

(form
  :type-tag      "Form/v1"
  :name          "forest_dissolve_subtree_postorder"
  :declared-caps (S-05/FOREST_RW)
  :declared-traps (ETYPE)
  :arity         2
  :locals-n      6
  :code (
    STORE   0                            ; locals[0] := root_h
    STORE   1                            ; locals[1] := att_id

    ;; Absent subtree ⇒ idempotent no-op: Pair{root, []}.
    LOAD    0
    LOAD    1
    PUSH    "Forest/hamt_lookup"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=2                     ; → Pair{Bool, Hash}
    FST
    JMPZ    +dissolve_absent

    ;; Present: hand off to the postorder recursion.
    LOAD    0
    LOAD    1
    PUSH    "Forest/dissolve_rec"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=2                     ; → Pair{ForestRoot, Vec{AttId}}
    RET

    :dissolve_absent
    LOAD    0
    PUSH    0
    MAKEVEC 0                            ; empty Vec{AttId}
    MAKEPAIR
    RET
  )
  :rationale-hash $$BLAKE3$$/forest-rationale
)

; ============================================================
; S-05/forest/deduct
;
; Reads the record at att_id, checks budget_remaining >= amount
; (else EOVERBUDGET), produces a new record with
; budget_remaining -= amount, re-inserts, returns the new root.
;
; Pseudocode:
;
;   deduct(root, att_id, amount):
;     (found, rec_h) = Forest/hamt_lookup(root, att_id)
;     if not found: trap EUNHELD
;     rec = read(rec_h)
;     if rec.budget_remaining < amount: trap EOVERBUDGET
;     rec'   = AttentionRecord/with_budget_sub(rec, amount)
;     rec_h' = Forest/seal_record(rec')
;     return Forest/hamt_insert_record(root, att_id, rec_h')
; ============================================================

(form
  :type-tag      "Form/v1"
  :name          "forest_deduct"
  :declared-caps (S-05/FOREST_RW)
  :declared-traps (ETYPE EUNHELD EOVERBUDGET)
  :arity         3
  :locals-n      10
  :code (
    STORE   0                            ; locals[0] := root_h
    STORE   1                            ; locals[1] := att_id
    STORE   2                            ; locals[2] := amount (Nat)

    LOAD    0
    LOAD    1
    PUSH    "Forest/hamt_lookup"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=2                     ; → Pair{Bool, Hash}
    STORE   3
    LOAD    3
    FST
    JMPZ    +deduct_absent
    LOAD    3
    SND
    STORE   4                            ; locals[4] := rec_h
    JMP     +deduct_present

    :deduct_absent
    TRAP    EUNHELD

    :deduct_present
    LOAD    4
    READ
    STORE   5                            ; locals[5] := rec bytes

    ;; Budget guard.
    LOAD    5
    PUSH    "S-05/proj/budget_remaining"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=1                     ; → budget_remaining (Nat)
    LOAD    2                            ; amount
    LT                                   ; (budget < amount)?
    JMPZ    +deduct_ok
    TRAP    EOVERBUDGET

    :deduct_ok
    LOAD    5                            ; rec
    LOAD    2                            ; amount
    PUSH    "AttentionRecord/with_budget_sub"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=2                     ; → rec' bytes
    PUSH    "Forest/seal_record"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=1                     ; → rec_h'
    STORE   6
    LOAD    0                            ; root
    LOAD    1                            ; att_id
    LOAD    6                            ; rec_h'
    PUSH    "Forest/hamt_insert_record"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=3                     ; → new root
    RET
  )
  :rationale-hash $$BLAKE3$$/forest-rationale
)

; ============================================================
; S-05/forest/mark_yielded
;
; Sets the leaf's yielded field to the continuation hash, and
; updates the inner AttentionRecord so the two stay in sync (the
; ForestLeaf duplicates yielded for cheap lookup, Forest.md
; § ForestLeaf/v1). Traps EUNHELD if att_id is absent.
;
; Pseudocode:
;
;   mark_yielded(root, att_id, cont_h):
;     (found, rec_h) = Forest/hamt_lookup(root, att_id)
;     if not found: trap EUNHELD
;     rec    = read(rec_h)
;     rec'   = AttentionRecord/with_yielded(rec, cont_h)
;     rec_h' = Forest/seal_record(rec')
;     return Forest/hamt_insert_record(root, att_id, rec_h')
;
; hamt_insert_record rebuilds the ForestLeaf, which copies the
; record's yielded into the leaf's yielded — keeping the two in
; sync is the insert sub-helper's invariant, proven there.
; ============================================================

(form
  :type-tag      "Form/v1"
  :name          "forest_mark_yielded"
  :declared-caps (S-05/FOREST_RW)
  :declared-traps (ETYPE EUNHELD)
  :arity         3
  :locals-n      10
  :code (
    STORE   0                            ; locals[0] := root_h
    STORE   1                            ; locals[1] := att_id
    STORE   2                            ; locals[2] := cont_h (Hash)

    LOAD    0
    LOAD    1
    PUSH    "Forest/hamt_lookup"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=2                     ; → Pair{Bool, Hash}
    STORE   3
    LOAD    3
    FST
    JMPZ    +yield_absent
    LOAD    3
    SND
    STORE   4                            ; locals[4] := rec_h
    JMP     +yield_present

    :yield_absent
    TRAP    EUNHELD

    :yield_present
    LOAD    4
    READ
    STORE   5                            ; locals[5] := rec bytes

    LOAD    5                            ; rec
    LOAD    2                            ; cont_h
    PUSH    "AttentionRecord/with_yielded"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=2                     ; → rec' bytes
    PUSH    "Forest/seal_record"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=1                     ; → rec_h'
    STORE   6
    LOAD    0                            ; root
    LOAD    1                            ; att_id
    LOAD    6                            ; rec_h'
    PUSH    "Forest/hamt_insert_record"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=3                     ; → new root
    RET
  )
  :rationale-hash $$BLAKE3$$/forest-rationale
)

; ============================================================
; S-05/forest/set_deadline
;
; Reads the record, produces a new one with the new deadline,
; re-inserts. Deadlines are weave-entry-count offsets; this helper
; does no arithmetic on them (Forest.md § set_deadline).
;
; Pseudocode:
;
;   set_deadline(root, att_id, new_deadline):
;     (found, rec_h) = Forest/hamt_lookup(root, att_id)
;     if not found: trap EUNHELD
;     rec    = read(rec_h)
;     rec'   = AttentionRecord/with_deadline(rec, new_deadline)
;     rec_h' = Forest/seal_record(rec')
;     return Forest/hamt_insert_record(root, att_id, rec_h')
; ============================================================

(form
  :type-tag      "Form/v1"
  :name          "forest_set_deadline"
  :declared-caps (S-05/FOREST_RW)
  :declared-traps (ETYPE EUNHELD)
  :arity         3
  :locals-n      10
  :code (
    STORE   0                            ; locals[0] := root_h
    STORE   1                            ; locals[1] := att_id
    STORE   2                            ; locals[2] := new_deadline (Nat)

    LOAD    0
    LOAD    1
    PUSH    "Forest/hamt_lookup"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=2                     ; → Pair{Bool, Hash}
    STORE   3
    LOAD    3
    FST
    JMPZ    +deadline_absent
    LOAD    3
    SND
    STORE   4                            ; locals[4] := rec_h
    JMP     +deadline_present

    :deadline_absent
    TRAP    EUNHELD

    :deadline_present
    LOAD    4
    READ
    STORE   5                            ; locals[5] := rec bytes

    LOAD    5                            ; rec
    LOAD    2                            ; new_deadline
    PUSH    "AttentionRecord/with_deadline"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=2                     ; → rec' bytes
    PUSH    "Forest/seal_record"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=1                     ; → rec_h'
    STORE   6
    LOAD    0                            ; root
    LOAD    1                            ; att_id
    LOAD    6                            ; rec_h'
    PUSH    "Forest/hamt_insert_record"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=3                     ; → new root
    RET
  )
  :rationale-hash $$BLAKE3$$/forest-rationale
)

(exports
  (forest_get                        (ForestRoot, AttId)                  → AttentionRecord)
  (forest_new_child                  (AttId, Nat, CapId)                  → AttId)
  (forest_atomic_split               (ForestRoot, AttId, Nat, AttId, Nat) → ForestRoot)
  (forest_dissolve_subtree_postorder (ForestRoot, AttId)                  → Pair{ForestRoot, Vec{AttId}})
  (forest_deduct                     (ForestRoot, AttId, Nat)             → ForestRoot)
  (forest_mark_yielded               (ForestRoot, AttId, Hash)            → ForestRoot)
  (forest_set_deadline               (ForestRoot, AttId, Nat)             → ForestRoot))

; ============================================================
; Pending sub-helpers introduced by this batch
;
; The bodies above delegate to fourteen new sub-helpers that
; constitute the schema layer for the attention forest. They are
; catalogued in STUBS.md as pending under the S-05 section and will
; be encoded in the next v0.2.0-helpers batch (forest-schema.form):
;
;   Forest/hamt_lookup                       (ForestRoot, AttId) → Pair{Bool, Hash}
;   Forest/hamt_insert_record                (ForestRoot, AttId, Hash) → ForestRoot
;   Forest/hamt_remove                       (ForestRoot, AttId) → ForestRoot
;   Forest/derive_att_id                     (AttId, Nat, CapId) → AttId
;   Forest/seal_record                       (AttentionRecord) → Hash
;   Forest/dissolve_rec                      (ForestRoot, AttId) → Pair{ForestRoot, Vec{AttId}}
;   AttentionRecord/proj/children            (AttentionRecord) → Vec{AttId}
;   AttentionRecord/proj/deadline            (AttentionRecord) → Nat
;   AttentionRecord/proj/yielded             (AttentionRecord) → Hash
;   AttentionRecord/construct_child          (AttId, AttentionRecord, Nat, Nat) → AttentionRecord
;   AttentionRecord/with_budget_sub_and_child (AttentionRecord, Nat, AttId) → AttentionRecord
;   AttentionRecord/with_budget_sub          (AttentionRecord, Nat) → AttentionRecord
;   AttentionRecord/with_deadline            (AttentionRecord, Nat) → AttentionRecord
;   AttentionRecord/with_yielded             (AttentionRecord, Hash) → AttentionRecord
;
; The Forest/hamt_* helpers are themselves layered: they share the
; HAMT bitmap/popcount arithmetic with Trie/branch_* (Trie.md), but
; parameterised on ForestLeaf/v1 leaves (att_id ‖ record ‖ yielded)
; rather than TrieLeaf/v1. The forest-schema batch reuses the
; trie-schema primitives wherever the node shape is identical and
; only adds the ForestLeaf projections/constructors and the
; budget_sum maintenance (Forest.md § ForestBranch/v1).
;
; Until those sub-helpers exist, the seven forest operations above
; have pending leaves at every inner CALL, per the layered-encoding
; convention. This file establishes the shape S-05's body sees and
; the .proof artifacts compose against.
; ============================================================

; ============================================================
; Proof obligations (drafted; full discharge in forest.proof)
;
; O1. Presence discipline. get / atomic_split / deduct /
;     mark_yielded / set_deadline all begin with Forest/hamt_lookup
;     and TRAP EUNHELD on the absent branch before any record is
;     constructed. dissolve_subtree_postorder treats absence as the
;     identity (idempotent, returns Pair{root, []}). There is no
;     path that reads or rebuilds a record for an AttId the forest
;     does not hold.
;
; O2. Budget safety (I6). atomic_split and deduct both guard with
;     `budget_remaining < amount → TRAP EOVERBUDGET` BEFORE sealing
;     any new record, and the only Nat subtraction happens inside
;     AttentionRecord/with_budget_sub{,_and_child}, which is reached
;     only after the guard passes. Therefore no operation drives a
;     record's budget_remaining negative, and budget_sum at the root
;     is non-increasing except across a mint (Forest.md § digest,
;     self-test vector #4). Composes against the sub-helpers'
;     "budget_sum = Σ leaf.budget_remaining" obligation.
;
; O3. Atomicity. atomic_split produces exactly one new ForestRoot
;     observable to any caller: the two Forest/hamt_insert_record
;     calls thread root → root' → root'' on the operand stack and
;     locals, and neither input root substance is mutated (no WRITE,
;     no MINT). A trap on either guard leaves the original root
;     untouched. There is no public Form that returns root'.
;
; O4. Determinism / replayability. new_child derives the child
;     AttId purely from (parent, index, focus) via Forest/derive_att_id
